{
  "id": "Compound::DB00835 - Gene::1555",
  "verbalization": "Brompheniramine, a nasal decongestant, is shown to bind to multiple cytochrome P450 enzymes—Cyp2e1, Cyp2c19, and Cyp2d6—each of which participates in steroid hydroxylase activity. This activity is then linked to the participation of Cyp2b6, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Brompheniramine may influence the activity of Cyp2b6. The shared involvement of these enzymes in steroid hydroxylase activity implies that Brompheniramine may modulate the metabolic processing of steroid hormones through these pathways. The cumulative evidence from the three paths supports a mechanistic link between Brompheniramine and Cyp2b6, particularly through the indirect influence of these enzymes. The observed scores suggest a consistent and plausible relationship, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct effect of Brompheniramine on Cyp2b6.",
